<title>SOUTH KOREA: LG INTERNATIONAL TO IMPORT NORTH KOREAN NAPHTHA.</title>
<headline>LG INTERNATIONAL TO IMPORT NORTH KOREAN NAPHTHA.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>LG International Corp, a trading unit of South Korea's LG Group, said on Monday it would import 12,000 tonnes of naphtha or $2.4 million worth from North Korea.</p>
<p>An LG official said the raw material for petrochemical products would arrive at a South Korean port on Tuesday.</p>
<p>LG plans to expand imports of North Korean petrochemical goods gradually if the quality of the naphtha turns out to be good, the company said.</p>
<p>North Korea usually imports crude oil from China and Russia.</p>
</text>
